mitigations/MIT-000078-interpreter-entry:
schema_version: "2.0.0"
type: mitigation
id: MIT-000078
name: {zh: 解释器入口、能力与内容审计治理, en: Interpreter Entry Capability and Content-Audit Governance}
summary: {zh: 以最小解释器入口、应用控制、受限语言/会话、脚本信任和受保护内容审计，减少正常谱系借用与短驻语义空间。, en: Reduce normal-lineage borrowing and transient semantics through least interpreter entry application control constrained language or sessions script trust and protected content auditing.}
description:
  paragraphs:
  - zh: 本缓解不主张按名称全面禁用解释器，因为管理、构建和应用工作流常依赖它们。控制应把谁能从何入口调用哪种能力，与批准脚本/模块、目录、网络目的地、资产范围和时间绑定；对支持的平台使用应用控制、签名策略、PowerShell ConstrainedLanguage/JEA、最小 RBAC 或等价受限执行环境，并启用可保护的脚本块、运行时与进程审计。
    en: This mitigation does not recommend disabling interpreters by name because operations, builds, and applications depend on them. Controls bind who can invoke which capability through what entry to approved scripts or modules, directories, network destinations, asset scope, and time. Where supported, use application control, signing policy, PowerShell ConstrainedLanguage or JEA, least RBAC, or equivalent constrained environments, and enable protected script-block, runtime, and process auditing.
  - zh: 控制目标是让攻击者无法仅凭签名解释器或正常父体获得全语言能力，让 stdin、管道与内存输入也进入审计和策略，并把例外限制在具体身份、内容与有效期。日志可能包含秘密，必须加密、最小访问和设置保留期；响应时先保存入口、内容指纹和结果谱系，再终止会话与撤销相关令牌。
    en: The objective is to prevent a signed interpreter or normal parent alone from conferring full-language capability, bring standard input, pipelines, and memory-fed content into audit and policy, and constrain exceptions to concrete identity, content, and validity. Logs may contain secrets and require encryption, least access, and retention limits. During response preserve entry, content fingerprint, and outcome lineage before terminating sessions and revoking related tokens.
domains: [enterprise]
measures:
- key: interpreter-entry-least-privilege
  name: {zh: 解释器入口最小权限, en: Interpreter Entry Least Privilege}
  description: {paragraphs: [{zh: 盘点用户、服务、Office/应用插件、管理代理、构建器和远程接口对解释器的调用路径，删除无业务需要入口，并把允许主体绑定到资产、目录、脚本/模块和目的地。, en: Inventory user service Office or application plug-in management-agent builder and remote-interface paths to interpreters remove entries without business need and bind allowed principals to assets directories scripts or modules and destinations.}]}
  control_type: exposure-reduction
- key: interpreter-capability-and-trust
  name: {zh: 解释器能力与内容信任约束, en: Interpreter Capability and Content Trust Constraints}
  description: {paragraphs: [{zh: 以应用控制、签名/哈希、受限语言、JEA 或沙箱把未批准脚本与内联内容限制为最小能力；批准例外使用具体内容身份与到期时间，不能永久放行解释器二进制。, en: Use application control signature or hash constrained language JEA or sandboxing to limit unapproved scripts and inline content to least capability; bind approved exceptions to concrete content identity and expiry rather than permanently allowing an interpreter binary.}]}
  control_type: preventive
- key: transient-content-audit
  name: {zh: 短驻内容与结果审计, en: Transient Content and Outcome Audit}
  description: {paragraphs: [{zh: 启用 Script Block/AMSI、runtime audit、execve 与完整进程谱系，记录 stdin/管道来源和网络取得内容的受保护指纹，并把调用与结果连接；对敏感原文加密和字段级授权。, en: Enable Script Block or AMSI runtime audit execve and complete process lineage record standard-input or pipeline origin and protected fingerprints of network-fetched content and join invocation to outcome; encrypt sensitive raw content and apply field-level authorization.}]}
  control_type: detective-support
- key: interpreter-session-response
  name: {zh: 解释器会话证据化响应, en: Evidence-Preserving Interpreter Session Response}
  description: {paragraphs: [{zh: 发现异常时保存祖先、主体、命令/内容哈希、模块、网络与子进程，随后终止会话、撤销令牌、隔离入口并按批准基线恢复；不得只删除临时文件。, en: On anomaly preserve ancestry principal command or content hash modules network and child processes then terminate the session revoke tokens isolate the entry and restore from an approved baseline; do not only delete temporary files.}]}
  control_type: containment
applications:
- target_ref: NJT-0065
  use: {paragraphs: [{zh: 建立解释器入口清单和按资产职责的允许矩阵，对未批准来源或内容实施受限能力，并统一采集入口—语义—结果链。对必须使用的解释器不做名称级放行，变更需要具体脚本/模块、主体、目标和有效期审批。, en: Maintain an interpreter-entry inventory and asset-role allowance matrix constrain unapproved origins or content and collect a unified entry-semantics-outcome chain. Do not allow required interpreters by name; changes require approval for concrete script or module principal target and validity.}]}
  expected_effect: {paragraphs: [{zh: 缩小可借用入口和可执行能力，使恶意指令必须触发策略差异或留下可关联内容，同时保留合法管理与构建功能。, en: Narrows borrowable entries and executable capability forcing malicious instructions to trigger a policy difference or leave correlatable content while preserving legitimate operations and builds.}]}
  limitations: {paragraphs: [{zh: 异构解释器能力不同，完整内容日志可能泄露秘密；被攻陷的批准脚本、签名者或管理代理仍可产生一致元数据，需要完整性与结果检测配合。, en: Heterogeneous interpreters expose different controls and full-content logs can leak secrets; a compromised approved script signer or management agent can still produce consistent metadata requiring integrity and outcome detection.}]}
- target_ref: NJS-0065-001
  use: {paragraphs: [{zh: 将允许项绑定完整祖先、主体、目录、脚本/模块哈希、目的地和资产角色；WMI、服务、Office 与管理代理只能调用明确列出的解释能力，偏离时降权或阻断。, en: Bind allowances to full ancestry principal directory script or module hash destination and asset role; WMI services Office and management agents may invoke only explicitly listed interpreter capabilities with divergence constrained or blocked.}]}
  expected_effect: {paragraphs: [{zh: 正常父级和签名不再足以掩护任意指令，攻击者必须同时破坏或复制更多独立控制面。, en: A normal parent and signature no longer shelter arbitrary instructions and the adversary must compromise or reproduce more independent control surfaces.}]}
  limitations: {paragraphs: [{zh: 动态运维和构建会频繁变化，过窄允许矩阵可能中断业务；应使用到期例外和审计模式逐步收敛。, en: Dynamic operations and builds change frequently and an overly narrow matrix can interrupt business; converge through expiring exceptions and audit mode.}]}
- target_ref: NJS-0065-002
  use: {paragraphs: [{zh: 对 stdin、`-Command`、管道、下载字符串和内存脚本启用运行时内容检查或默认受限能力；若业务需要内联，要求受控主体、内容指纹、目的地与审批，并保留结果谱系。, en: Apply runtime content inspection or constrained capability by default to standard input command parameters pipelines downloaded strings and memory scripts; when inline use is required bind principal content fingerprint destination and approval and retain outcome lineage.}]}
  expected_effect: {paragraphs: [{zh: 把策略和检测移动到短驻语义存在的时点，使无独立脚本不能绕过能力控制或调查链。, en: Moves policy and detection to the moment transient semantics exist so absence of a standalone script cannot bypass capability control or the investigative chain.}]}
  limitations: {paragraphs: [{zh: 某些嵌入运行时不暴露完整内容，关闭内联能力会影响安装器与自动化；日志脱敏或哈希可能降低事后解释能力。, en: Some embedded runtimes do not expose complete content and disabling inline capability can affect installers and automation; redaction or hashing can reduce post-incident interpretation.}]}
evidence_refs: [REF-000198, REF-000199, REF-000200, REF-000201]
