mitigations/MIT-000094-wmi-namespace-met:
schema_version: 2.0.0
type: mitigation
id: MIT-000094
name: {zh: WMI Namespace、Method 与来源谱系治理, en: WMI Namespace Method and Provenance-Lineage Governance}
summary: {zh: 通过最小 WMI 权限、受管远程来源、Operation tracing、方法准入和 Wmiprvse 结果控制降低 WMI 执行滥用, en: Reduce WMI execution abuse through least WMI authority managed remote origins operation tracing method admission and Wmiprvse outcome controls}
description: {paragraphs: [{zh: 本缓解保留 WMI 的管理价值，但按角色限制 namespace 和 execution-capable method，强制远程认证/加密/来源，启用 client-to-provider operation tracing，并对 Wmiprvse child/module/network 应用行为控制。目标是让 provider 托管不丢失原始身份，让常见管理方法不能成为全局白名单。, en: This mitigation preserves WMI management value while restricting namespaces and execution-capable methods by role enforcing remote authentication encryption and origins enabling client-to-provider operation tracing and applying behavioral controls to Wmiprvse children modules and network. Provider hosting must not lose original identity and common management methods cannot become global allowlists.}]}
domains: [enterprise]
measures:
  - {key: least-wmi-namespace-method, name: {zh: 最小 Namespace 与执行 Method 权限, en: Least Namespace and Execution-Method Authority}, description: {paragraphs: [{zh: 只向受管管理员/服务账户授予所需 namespace、class/method，单独限制 Win32_Process/ExecMethod、provider 注册和远程访问，移除共享账户与过宽 DCOM/WinRM 权限。, en: Grant only needed namespaces classes and methods to managed administrators or service accounts separately restrict Win32_Process or ExecMethod provider registration and remote access and remove shared accounts and broad DCOM or WinRM rights.}]}, control_type: preventive}
  - {key: managed-remote-wmi-origin, name: {zh: 受管远程 WMI 来源与认证, en: Managed Remote WMI Origins and Authentication}, description: {paragraphs: [{zh: 仅允许批准管理服务器通过 Kerberos/强认证和加密访问 WMI，限制端口/防火墙与 JIT，记录 source host、user、session 和 target。, en: Allow WMI only from approved management servers through Kerberos or strong authentication and encryption restrict ports firewalls and JIT and record source host user session and target.}]}, control_type: exposure-reduction}
  - {key: operation-lineage-and-provider-outcome, name: {zh: Operation 谱系与 Provider 结果控制, en: Operation Lineage and Provider-Outcome Control}, description: {paragraphs: [{zh: 启用 WMI-Activity/Trace 并集中保存 client/OperationId/provider，向 EDR 关联 Wmiprvse child/module/file/network；阻止 encoded shell、用户路径、未批准下载和 destructive method 结果。, en: Enable and centralize WMI-Activity or Trace client OperationId and provider data and join Wmiprvse children modules files and network in EDR while blocking encoded shells user paths unapproved downloads and destructive method outcomes.}]}, control_type: detective-support}
applications:
  - target_ref: NJT-0082
    use: {paragraphs: [{zh: 对匿迹化 WMI 执行，为所有 execution-capable operation 保留 client→method→provider→outcome 链，并用资产角色策略检查 source/principal/method/command。无 OperationId 或来自非管理源的高风险 method 转入阻断/隔离。, en: For Stealth-Conforming WMI Execution retain client-to-method-to-provider-to-outcome lineage for every execution-capable operation and check source principal method and command against asset-role policy while high-risk methods without OperationIds or from nonmanagement origins are blocked or isolated.}]}
    expected_effect: {paragraphs: [{zh: Wmiprvse 不再遮蔽原始发起者，常见管理身份与端口也不能覆盖 encoded command 或异常结果；远程横向和本地谱系打断成本上升。, en: Wmiprvse no longer hides original initiators and common management identities or ports cannot override encoded commands or anomalous outcomes raising costs for remote lateral movement and local lineage breaking.}]}
    limitations: {paragraphs: [{zh: WMI 广泛被 SCCM、监控和应用使用，方法级限制可能破坏业务；Trace 数据量大且 client PID 会重用，平台升级/WMIC 弃用要求持续映射。, en: WMI is broadly used by SCCM monitoring and applications and method restrictions may break business while Trace is high volume client PIDs are reused and platform changes or WMIC deprecation require ongoing mapping.}]}
  - target_ref: NJS-0082-001
    use: {paragraphs: [{zh: 对 Provider 宿主来源遮蔽，强制 WMI Trace 记录 ClientMachine/User/PID/OperationId，并在 provider child 创建时附加 operation context；Office/script/remote nonmanagement client 的 execution method 默认高风险。, en: For Provider-Hosted Execution-Provenance Masking require WMI Trace client machine user PID and OperationId and attach operation context to provider children while execution methods from Office scripts or remote nonmanagement clients default to high risk.}]}
    expected_effect: {paragraphs: [{zh: TA551 式 winword 谱系打断可还原，AvosLocker encoded PowerShell 能连接原始 WMI client/remote session，而非停在 Wmiprvse。, en: TA551-style Winword lineage breaks are recoverable and AvosLocker encoded PowerShell links to original WMI clients or remote sessions rather than stopping at Wmiprvse.}]}
    limitations: {paragraphs: [{zh: Legacy/第三方 provider 可能不提供完整 ID，自托管 provider 不使用 Wmiprvse；日志关闭或同一高权主体控制 tracing 时仍可失去来源。, en: Legacy or third-party providers may omit IDs and self-hosted providers do not use Wmiprvse while disabled logs or one privileged actor controlling tracing can still lose provenance.}]}
  - target_ref: NJS-0082-002
    use: {paragraphs: [{zh: 对日常管理情境合形，按管理平台和资产角色建立 namespace-class-method-principal-cadence 与允许结果基线，例外绑定 source host、service account、method、target role 和期限；不全局放行 WMIC、PowerShell 或 Wmiprvse。, en: For Routine-Administration Context Conformity baseline namespace class method principal cadence and allowed outcomes by management platform and asset role and bind exceptions to source host service account method target role and expiry without globally allowing WMIC PowerShell or Wmiprvse.}]}
    expected_effect: {paragraphs: [{zh: 恶意操作必须同时匹配实际管理源、权限和结果，借常见 class/account 不足以伪装，encoded command、异常下载或 destructive side effect 会触发差分。, en: Malicious operations must match real management origins authority and outcomes and common classes or accounts alone cannot disguise them while encoded commands anomalous downloads or destructive side effects create differentials.}]}
    limitations: {paragraphs: [{zh: 管理基线随软件和脚本变化，紧急响应会使用非常用 method；攻击者控制批准管理服务器可匹配 source/principal，因此仍需 command 与结果审查。, en: Management baselines change with software and scripts and emergency response uses unusual methods while adversaries controlling approved servers may match sources and principals so command and outcome review remains necessary.}]}
evidence_refs: [REF-000293, REF-000294, REF-000295]
